# Display-only identity mapping. Rewrites nothing in history — git applies this
# at read time (log, shortlog, blame), so old commits keep their original bytes.
#
# `git shortlog -sne` split one person across several contributors: 83 commits
# under the short handle with a capitalised address, 7 under the current one,
# and 2 more under an assistant identity on refs outside main.
#
# The school address is mapped pre-emptively — it appears nowhere in this
# repo's history today (checked with `git log --all`), but it is the same
# person and a commit from that machine would otherwise split the list again.
#
# Bot identities (dependabot[bot], github-actions[bot], GitHub <noreply@github.com>
# on web-UI merges) are deliberately left alone: they are honest about who acted.

